        <div class="era-stat"><span class="era-stat-label">Unique Composers</span><span class="era-stat-value">18</span></div>
        <div class="era-stat"><span class="era-stat-label">Repeat Win Rate</span><span class="era-stat-value">~35%</span></div>
        <div class="era-stat"><span class="era-stat-label">Top Repeat Winner</span><span class="era-stat-value">Alan Menken (3×), Williams (2×), Barry (2×)</span></div>
        <div class="era-composers">
          <strong>Defining figures:</strong> John Williams, Alan Menken, John Barry, Maurice Jarre, Hans Zimmer, James Horner.<br><br>
          The Modern Era saw the heaviest concentration of repeat victories of any period: 7 of 20 ceremonies went to composers who had already won. Alan Menken's three consecutive Disney animation wins (1989–1992) remain unmatched as a streak within a single genre. Synth-orchestral hybrids (Vangelis, Moroder's legacy) briefly threatened orchestral dominance, but Williams and Barry anchored a traditional core.
        </div>
